```python
@gene("m11", "the camp walk's goal: nearest safe spawn of a live group, falling back to any live group", parents=["m11"])
def camp_goal() -> Tile:
    easy = CAMP_BASE - respawning() - CAMP_HOT
    if size(easy) > 0:
        return closest(easy)
    return closest(CAMP_BASE - respawning())
```

The change is to `adj_altar` only. It now prefers an adjacent altar that no enemy lock blocks, and falls back to any adjacent altar. This makes the pre-fight bank more likely to succeed when a locked altar sits next to us.

```python
@gene("m2b", "an altar next to us, preferring one no enemy lock blocks", parents=["m2"])
def adj_altar() -> Tile:
    near_alt = altars() & near(here(), 1)
    open_alt = near_alt - locked_altars()
    if size(open_alt) > 0:
        return first_tile(open_alt)
    return first_tile(near_alt)
```

```python
@gene("r5", "recall with gems when hurt (threshold rises with the bag, ignoring tiny bags) and nothing near, unless an altar is close enough to bank first (closer allowed when badly hurt)")
def r_cashout() -> Bool:
    g = gems()
    if g <= 2 or at_spawn():
        return False
    if not hurt_below(0.42 + min(g, 50) / 200):
        return False
    if under_fire():
        return False
    eta = altar_eta()
    if hurt_below(0.3):
        return eta > 2
    return eta > 3
```

The change makes `fight_foe` skip enemies standing on their own spawn, so the bot picks the weakest attackable champion that is not camping spawn, instead of locking onto a spawn-camper and then failing `r_fight`'s spawn check.

```python
@gene("s13", "the weakest enemy champion in reach, skipping any standing on its own spawn")
def fight_foe() -> Unit:
    return best(enemies(), lambda u: -u.health if (in_reach(u) and not (u.pos in enemy_spawn())) else -INF)
```

```python
@gene("r7", "fight the weakest enemy champion in reach (not on its own spawn)", parents=["r7"])
def r_fight() -> Bool:
    f = fight_foe()
    return exists(f) and dist(here(), f.pos) <= me().attack_range and not (f.pos in enemy_spawn())
```
